3.3 Robustness of Neural SDE
In this section, we theoretically analyze the stability of Neural SDE, showing that the randomness term can indeed improve the robustness of the model against small input perturbation. This also explains why noise injection can improve the robustness in discrete networks, which has been observed in literature [6, 7]. First we need to show the existence and uniqueness of solution to (3), we pose following assumptions on drift f and diffusion G.
Assumption 1. f and G are at most linear, i.e. ‖f (x, t)‖ + ‖G(x, t)‖ ≤ c1(1 + ‖x‖) for c1 > 0, ∀x ∈ Rn and t ∈ R+.
